Theorem PL-8: TRMC candidate predicate — self-recursive + recursive call in tail position of a constructor argument + constructor in the return path; context region spans recursive call to wrapping constructor

  Preconditions:
    - The AIMS pipeline is a 12-step strictly-ordered sequence per
      Annex E §AIMS §6. PL-8 is the §07.4 TRMC
      candidate-predicate rule, refining PL-7's detection scope into the exact
      three-conjunct structural condition and the context-region span.
    - PL-8 statement (per Annex E §AIMS PL-8): the TRMC candidate
      predicate = self-recursive + recursive call in tail position of a
      constructor argument + constructor in the return path. The context
      region = span from the recursive call to the wrapping constructor.
    - PL-8 type signature (per Pipeline.proof lines 67-72, the sorry
      obligation this theorem discharges):
        type : Function -> Bool
        candidate = self-recursive + recursive call in tail position of
        constructor argument + constructor in return path; context region =
        span from recursive call to wrapping constructor.
    - Shipped candidate-predicate driver: the predicate is realized across two
      shipped components:
        (1) ori_arc::aims::normalize::collect_recursive_call_sites
            (compiler/ori_arc/src/aims/normalize/detect.rs, via
            ori_arc::aims::intraprocedural::post_convergence.rs lines 449-450)
            collects the self-recursive call sites — the SELF-RECURSIVE
            conjunct. `recursive_defs` is empty for non-self-recursive
            functions, short-circuiting detection (post_convergence.rs lines
            451-453).
        (2) ori_arc::aims::intraprocedural::post_convergence::
            detect_trmc_candidates (post_convergence.rs lines 469-497) requires
            a `Construct` (CONSTRUCTOR-IN-RETURN-PATH conjunct, lines 476-487)
            with a field argument produced by a recursive call
            (RECURSIVE-CALL-IN-CONSTRUCTOR-ARGUMENT conjunct, lines 493-497).
      A function passing all three is a TRMC candidate; failing any one is not.
    - Shipped context-region span: ori_arc::aims::contract::context::
      ContextRegion (compiler/ori_arc/src/aims/contract/
      context.rs lines 97-113) records the span:
        - `open_block` + `open_instr` (context.rs lines 100-102) — the block /
          instruction index of the `Construct` (context open);
        - `close_block` + `close_instr` (context.rs lines 107-110) — the block /
          instruction index of the `Apply`/`Invoke` that fills the hole
          (context close);
        - `context_var` (line 104), `hole_field` (line 106), `hole_var`
          (line 112) carry the constructor root, the hole field index, and the
          recursive-call result variable.
      Per the doc comment (context.rs lines 84-86): "The region spans from the
      constructor allocation (context open) to the recursive call that fills
      the hole (context close)."
    - The context region is produced by ori_arc::aims::normalize::
      detect_context_regions (normalize/mod.rs line 96, re-exported from
      detect.rs at normalize/mod.rs line 43) and consumed by
      intraprocedural::analyze_function to record ContextOpen / ContextClose
      events (context.rs lines 88-90).

  Soundness property:
    Forall function F.
      Let candidate(F) = F is a TRMC candidate per Step 3a detection.
      Two conjuncts SHALL hold:

      (P1) Predicate conjunction:
        candidate(F) iff self_recursive(F)
                       AND recursive_call_in_constructor_arg(F)
                       AND constructor_in_return_path(F).
        Dropping ANY one of the three structural conditions makes F not a
        candidate.

      (P2) Context-region span well-formedness:
        For every detected candidate, the ContextRegion (open_block,
        open_instr) -> (close_block, close_instr) brackets the recursive call
        inside the wrapping constructor with addressable, distinct endpoints
        (distinct positions OR distinct blocks). A degenerate region (same
        block AND same instruction for open and close) is not well-formed.

  Proof obligation:
    Two-part constructive discharge corresponding to (P1) and (P2), by
    case analysis over the three-conjunct truth table (case_analysis-led per
    the §00 PL row) + structural confirmation of the region span.

    Part (P1) — Predicate conjunction (case analysis over the truth table):

      The verifier models the shipped candidate predicate as the conjunction
        pl8_is_candidate(c) = c.self_recursive
                              AND c.recursive_call_in_ctor_arg
                              AND c.ctor_in_return_path
      and exercises it over four cases — the all-hold case plus one
      single-conjunct-drop case per conjunct:

        Case all_three_hold — all conjuncts true -> CANDIDATE
        Case not_self_recursive — drop conjunct 1 -> NOT
        Case recursive_call_not_in_ctor_arg — drop conjunct 2 -> NOT
        Case no_ctor_in_return_path — drop conjunct 3 -> NOT

      Each negative case maps to a shipped short-circuit:
        - not_self_recursive: collect_recursive_call_sites returns an empty set,
          so detect_trmc_candidates returns early (post_convergence.rs lines
          451-453) — no candidate;
        - recursive_call_not_in_ctor_arg: the Construct's args do not contain a
          recursive-call result, so the `has_recursive_arg` guard fails
          (post_convergence.rs lines 493-497) — `continue`, no candidate;
        - no_ctor_in_return_path: there is no `Construct` to inspect (plain tail
          recursion), so the per-Construct scan finds nothing
          (post_convergence.rs lines 469-487) — no candidate.

      For each case the verifier asserts pl8_is_candidate agrees with the
      expected result. The case-by-case agreement discharges (P1).

    Part (P2) — Context-region span well-formedness (structural confirmation):

      The verifier checks the region span via pl8_region_span_well_formed,
      modeling the shipped ContextRegion endpoints (open_block, open_instr,
      close_block, close_instr; context.rs lines 100-110). The span is
      well-formed iff the endpoints are addressable and distinct — distinct
      blocks OR distinct instruction indices. A representative region (Construct
      at open block 1 instruction 2; recursive call producing the hole value at
      close block 0 instruction 0) is verified well-formed; a degenerate region
      (open block 0 instr 0 == close block 0 instr 0) is verified NOT
      well-formed. The recursive call result fills the hole, so close_instr may
      precede the wrapping Construct in instruction order (the value is
      computed, then wrapped) or follow it (forward-filled hole) — the span is
      well-formed in either ordering provided the endpoints are addressable and
      distinct. (P2) discharged.

    Coverage gate — candidate-predicate case enumeration:

      The verifier discharges exactly 4 candidate-predicate cases
      (require_count("PL-8", 4, ...)). Coverage axes:
        Predicate conjunction (P1): the 4 truth-table cases — 1 candidate (all
          conjuncts hold) + 3 rejections (one per dropped conjunct).
        Region span (P2): the well-formed representative region + the
          degenerate-region negative pin.

    Negative-direction witness — single dropped conjunct rejects:

      The candidate predicate is a strict three-way conjunction: dropping
      self-recursion (no recursive call), or moving the recursive call out of a
      constructor argument's tail position, or removing the wrapping
      constructor from the return path (plain tail recursion) each independently
      blocks candidacy. The verifier's three negative cases pin each dropped
      conjunct against its shipped short-circuit.

    Negative-direction witness — degenerate region rejected:

      A region whose open and close endpoints coincide (same block AND same
      instruction) does not bracket a recursive call inside a constructor — it
      is not a well-formed context region. The verifier's degenerate-region
      check (open b0.i0 == close b0.i0 -> not well-formed) pins this.

    Cycle-soundness witness — PL-8 sits between PL-7 and PL-9:

      PL-8 (candidate predicate + region span) refines PL-7's detection scope
      and is the antecedent of PL-9 (rewrite of the detected candidate's
      context region). Its antecedent is PL-7 (which establishes the detection
      filter and the ContextHole shape the predicate selects). PL-8 consumes no
      output of PL-9 / PL-10 / PL-11. The dependency chain is acyclic:
        PL-7 --> PL-8 (predicate refines the detection conjunction)
        PL-8 --> PL-9 (rewrite of the detected candidate region)
      No cycle.

    Algorithm-citation declaration:
      property: TRMC candidate predicate — a function is a candidate
                           iff self-recursive AND recursive call in tail
                           position of a constructor argument AND constructor in
                           the return path; the context region spans the
                           recursive call to the wrapping constructor
      published: Leijen & Lorenzen, "Tail Recursion Modulo Context",
                           JFP 2025 (the tail-modulo-cons candidate shape: a
                           self-recursive call appearing under a constructor in
                           tail position defines the constructor context)
      determinism: deterministic — collect_recursive_call_sites + the
                           per-Construct scan apply a fixed three-conjunct
                           filter in block / instruction order; the region span
                           is a fixed (open, close) pair of IR positions
      reference impl: ori_arc::aims::normalize::collect_recursive_call_sites
                           (self-recursive conjunct, via post_convergence.rs
                           lines 449-453) + ori_arc::aims::intraprocedural::
                           post_convergence::detect_trmc_candidates
                           (constructor-in-return + recursive-call-in-arg
                           conjuncts, post_convergence.rs lines 469-497) +
                           ori_arc::aims::contract::context::ContextRegion span
                           (context.rs lines 97-113)

    Engines dispatched:
      structural_induction (PRIMARY — confirms the predicate conjunction and
        the region-span well-formedness over the §07.4 TRMC structural model
        per section_07::verify_pl8_trmc_candidate_predicate; agrees with
        case_analysis on the constructive verifier)
      case_analysis (LED — per the §00 PL-row pair per the proof-checker design-proof-
        checker-design.md:102, the TRMC cluster is case_analysis-heavy; the
        verifier discharges (P1) via the four-row predicate truth table — 1
        candidate + 3 single-conjunct-drop rejections — and (P2) via the
        well-formed-vs-degenerate region-span check; constructive, NOT
        gracious-accept)

  Expected:
    status: valid
    reason: section_07 case_analysis-led discharge of PL-8 via the candidate-predicate truth table — (P1) a function is a TRMC candidate iff self-recursive (collect_recursive_call_sites non-empty, post_convergence.rs lines 449-453) AND recursive call in a constructor argument (lines 493-497) AND constructor in the return path (lines 476-487), verified over a four-row table (1 candidate + 3 single-conjunct-drop rejections), and (P2) the ContextRegion span (open_block/open_instr -> close_block/close_instr, context.rs lines 97-113) brackets the recursive call inside the wrapping constructor with addressable distinct endpoints (degenerate same-block-same-instr region rejected); structural_induction PRIMARY confirms over the same verifier
